# galleries: the Delvers' galleries under the fells, where they followed the star-iron down and sealed what they found.
@art deep
@kind mine
@ground fell peak heath
@seen a timbered adit
@names hold, gate, deep, mountain, keep
@danger 2
--- outside
  Observe {w}_adit_seen at {w} when true "An adit goes into the fellside, square and low, its frame of black oak beams. Spoil heaps run down the slope below it, grassed over long ago.".
  Observe {w}_cut at {w} when true "A name is cut in the lintel beam, in the old script, with a hammer and a star beside it: {oldup}." teaches {w}_named.
  Thing {w}_beam "the letters on the lintel beam" at {w} {
    State unread "Letters are cut in the lintel beam in the old script, beside a hammer and a star.".
    State read "{oldup}, the beam says, “{gloss}”; the hammer and the star were the Delvers' mark on whatever they claimed.".
    Change read "Read the letters on the lintel beam" from unread to read needing lore.
  }
--- base
  Place {w}_site "{name}" is site within {land} at {x}, {y}.
  Place {w}_works "the upper galleries" is level within {w}_site.
  Place {w}_deep "the deep galleries" is level within {w}_site.
  Place {w}_adit "the adit gallery" is room within {w}_works at 0, 0.
  Place {w}_head "the lift-head" is room within {w}_works at 1, 0.
  Place {w}_fall "the fallen gallery" is room within {w}_works at 1, 1.
  Place {w}_foot "the foot of the shaft" is room within {w}_deep at 0, 0.
  Place {w}_dressing "the dressing-hall" is room within {w}_deep at 1, 0.
  Place {w}_door_room "the end of the last gallery" is room within {w}_deep at 2, 0.
  Place {w}_vein "the pale vein" is room within {w}_works at 2, 1.
  Passage {w}_in "the adit mouth" is drift between {w} and {w}_adit.
  Passage {w}_on "the railed gallery" is passage between {w}_adit and {w}_head.
  Passage {w}_side "the side gallery" is passage between {w}_head and {w}_fall.
  Passage {w}_shaft "the lift shaft" is shaft between {w}_head and {w}_foot.
  Passage {w}_low "the low gallery" is passage between {w}_foot and {w}_dressing.
  Passage {w}_last "the last gallery" is passage between {w}_dressing and {w}_door_room.
  Passage {w}_through "the gap in the fall" is crawl between {w}_fall and {w}_vein.
  Observe {w}_adit_scene at {w}_adit when true "Rails of iron, black and flaking, run back into the hill on sleepers of oak. The walls are cut square and smooth; the Delvers did not hurry.".
  Observe {w}_head_scene at {w}_head when true "The gallery ends at a square shaft going straight down into the dark. Over it hangs a frame of iron beams with a great wheel at the top, and chains running down.".
  Observe {w}_fall_scene at {w}_fall when true "A side gallery runs a little way and ends in a fall of rock from roof to floor. Cold air comes through the gaps.".
  Observe {w}_foot_scene at {w}_foot when true "The bottom of the shaft opens on a gallery cut through rock so hard it rings. Far above, a square of grey that is the lift-head.".
  Observe {w}_dressing_scene at {w}_dressing when true "A long hall where the ore was broken and sorted: stone tables, troughs, hammers rusted to the stone. In a corner, a furnace of fire-brick, cold for a thousand years.".
  Observe {w}_door_scene at {w}_door_room when true "The last gallery ends at a door of iron set into the rock, taller than two men. Three bars as thick as a man's leg lie across it in iron hasps, on this side. The air by it is cold enough to see your breath.".
  Observe {w}_vein_scene at {w}_vein when true "Beyond the fall the gallery follows a vein of something pale through the rock, glinting where your light touches it.".
  Thing {w}_cage "the iron lift-cage" on {w}_shaft {
    State jammed blocking "The lift-cage is somewhere at the bottom of the shaft; its chains are rusted fast on the great wheel.".
    State working "The lift-cage rides the shaft on its chains, groaning, the counterweight going up as it goes down.".
    Change free "Break the rust off the wheel and wind the lift-cage up" from jammed to working needing brawn.
  }
  Initially Assert unlit({w}_adit). Initially Assert unlit({w}_head). Initially Assert unlit({w}_fall).
  Initially Assert unlit({w}_foot). Initially Assert unlit({w}_dressing). Initially Assert unlit({w}_door_room).
  Initially Assert unlit({w}_vein).
  Thing {w}_rubble "the fall of rock" on {w}_through {
    State fallen blocking "The fall fills the gallery; you could dig through it, with the means.".
    State dug "A gap has been dug through the fall, low enough to crawl.".
    Change dig "Dig through the fall" from fallen to dug needing digging or shovel.
  }
  Place {w}_beyond "the dark behind the iron door" is room within {w}_deep at 3, 0.
  Passage {w}_iron "the iron door" is door between {w}_door_room and {w}_beyond.
  Thing {w}_bars "the bars across the iron door" on {w}_iron {
    State set blocking "Three great bars lie across the iron door in their hasps.".
    State lifted "The bars have been lifted from the iron door and stand against the wall.".
    Change lift "Lift the bars off the iron door" from set to lifted needing brawn.
  }
  Thing {w}_tally "a tally cut in the wall" at {w}_dressing {
    State unread "Columns of marks are cut in the wall by the furnace, in the old script, the last of them cut deeper than the rest.".
    State read "A tally of star-iron, cart by cart, for a hundred years; then a gap; then, cut deep and crooked: WE HAVE SHUT IT IN. DO NOT LET IT OUT.".
    Change read "Read the tally on the wall" from unread to read needing lore.
  }
  Observe {w}_tally_learned at {w}_dressing when state({w}_tally, read) "{craft} {fate}" teaches history_makers.
  Person {w}_cold "the cold below" at {w}_beyond {
    Role "something that was walled up behind the iron door, and is not dead". Species ice_elemental. Level 5. Temperament savage. Lair {w}_beyond.
  }
  Rule {w}_loosed when state({w}_bars, lifted) and at({w}_cold, {w}_beyond) says "The iron door swings open of its own weight, and the cold comes out of the dark behind it, and has a shape." { Retract at({w}_cold, {w}_beyond). Assert at({w}_cold, {w}_door_room). }
  Initially Assert unlit({w}_beyond).
  Observe {w}_beyond_scene at {w}_beyond when true "A gallery cut rougher than the rest, as if in a hurry, running down into the cold. The walls glitter with frost, and with the pale ore, thick as a man's arm.".
  Item {w}_deep_ore "{richname}" is {rich} at {w}_beyond.
  Item {w}_ore "{commonname}" is {common} at {w}_vein.
--- successors miners 2
  Observe {w}_miners at {w}_adit when true "Later miners worked the upper galleries for tin, and their rough pit-props stand among the Delvers' oak: the kingdom of {successors} took what it could reach. A crowbar lies where one of them left it.".
  Item {w}_crowbar "a miner's crowbar" is crowbar at {w}_adit.
--- successors grille 1
  Observe {w}_grille at {w}_adit when true "Someone fitted an iron grille across the gallery here, and someone else broke it open; it hangs from one hinge. Scratched into the rock beside it, in the folk's letters: KEEP OUT.".
--- successors forgotten 1
  Observe {w}_dust at {w}_adit when true "Nothing in the dust but the tracks of small animals.".
--- present spiders 2
  Person {w}_spiders "cave spiders" at {w}_head {
    Role "spiders as big as a cat, nesting in the frame over the shaft". Species cave_spider. Numbers 3. Level 1. Temperament ambush.
    Comes "Something drops out of the iron frame overhead, and then another.".
  }
--- present goblins 1
  Person {w}_goblins "goblins" at {w}_adit {
    Role "a band of goblins who have made a home of the upper galleries". Ancestry goblin. Calling thief. Numbers 3. Temperament wary. Refuge {w}_fall.
  }
--- present empty 2
  Observe {w}_quiet at {w}_head when true "Somewhere below, water drips. Nothing else moves.".
--- hook ore 2
  Topic {w}_hook with {merchant} "Ask {{merchant}} about the old workings" when not knows(actor, {w}_named) once {
    Says "'The Delvers' galleries at {name}, up in {where},' says {{merchant}}. 'Worked out, they say. They are not. Bring me what glints down there and I will pay you double what anyone in {townname} would.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {w}_named). Assert knows(actor, {w}_found). }
  }
  Initially Set pays({merchant}, {common}) to {premium}.
--- hook warning 1
  Topic {w}_hook with {teller} "Ask {{teller}} about the fells above {townname}" when not knows(actor, {w}_named) once {
    Says "'There are old workings up there in {where}: {name},' says {{teller}}. 'My grandfather went down them after the silver. He came back up, but he was never warm again, not in summer, not by the fire. Leave them be.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {w}_named). Assert knows(actor, {w}_found). }
  }
